of Stunting in Syrian Refugee Children With Cleft Lip and/or Cleft Palate in Time of Crisis: A Call for Intervention. Cleft Palate Craniofac J. 2020;57(10):1166–1170. doi: 10.1177/1055665620930450. doi:10.1177/1055665620930450. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Butali A, Adeyemo WL, Mossey PA, et al. Prevalence of orofacial clefts in Nigeria. Cleft Palate Craniofac J. 2014;51(3):320–325. doi: 10.1597/12-135. doi:10.1597/12-135. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Eshete M, Butali A, Deressa W, et al. Descriptive Epidemiology of Orofacial Clefts in Ethiopia. J Craniofac Surg. 2017;28(2):334–337. doi: 10.1097/SCS.0000000000003234. doi:10.1097/SCS.0000000000003234. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Agbenorku P, Yore M, Danso KA, Turpin C. Incidence of Orofacial Clefts in Kumasi, Ghana. ISRN Plast Surg. 2013;2013:1–6. [ Google Scholar ] 26. Shkoukani MA, Chen M, Vong A. Cleft lip - a comprehensive review. Front Pediatr. 2013;1:53. doi: 10.3389/fped.2013.00053. doi:10.3389/fped.2013.00053. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Wilson J, Hodges A. Cleft lip and palate surgery carried out by one team in Uganda: where have all the palates gone? Cleft Palate Craniofac J. 2012;49(3):299–304. doi: 10.1597/09-039. doi:10.1597/09-039. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Srinivasan CS, Zanello G, Shankar B. Rural-urban disparities in child nutrition in Bangladesh and Nepal. BMC Public Health. 2013;13:581. doi: 10.1186/1471-2458-13-581. doi:10.1186/1471-2458-13-581. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Fotso JC. Urban-rural differentials in child malnutrition: trends and socioeconomic correlates in sub-Saharan Africa. Health Place. 2007;13(1):205–223. doi: 10.1016/j.healthplace.2006.01.004. doi:10.1016/j.healthplace.2006.01.004. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supple