sponse monitoring of HPV-associated cancers; a meta-analysis on recurrent event endpoints. Cancer Med 2023; 12: 17592–17602. 20230726. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Li W, Dong M, Huang S, et al. Efficacy and safety of PEG-rhG-CSF in preventing chemoradiotherapy-induced neutropenia in patients with locally advanced cervical cancer. Biomol Biomed 2023; 23: 310–316. 20230316. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Nalbant E, Akkaya-Ulum YZ. Exploring regulatory mechanisms on miRNAs and their implications in inflammation-related diseases. Clin Exp Med 2024; 24: 42. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. Natarajan L, Pu M, Davies SR, et al. miRNAs and long-term breast cancer survival: evidence from the WHEL study. Cancer Epidemiol Biomarkers Prev 2019; 28: 1525–1533. 20190611. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 37. Zografos E, Zagouri F, Kalapanida D, et al. Prognostic role of microRNAs in breast cancer: a systematic review. Oncotarget 2019: 10: 7156. breast cancer; microRNAs; prognosis; biomarkers. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Supplementary Materials sj-docx-1-sci-10.1177_00368504251380636 - Supplemental material for Effects of chemoradiotherapy on plasma oncogenic miRNAs as biomarkers in cervical cancer patients: A prospective observational study sj-docx-1-sci-10.1177_00368504251380636.docx (61.2KB, docx) Supplemental material, sj-docx-1-sci-10.1177_00368504251380636 for Effects of chemoradiotherapy on plasma oncogenic miRNAs as biomarkers in cervical cancer patients: A prospective observational study by Masoumeh Parvizi, Mohammad Taghizadeh-Teymorloei, Maryam Vaezi, Masoumeh Bakhshandeh, Noushin Mobaraki-Asl, Ebrahim Esmati, Reza Eghdam-Zamiri, Farhad Jeddi and Abbas Karimi in Science Progress sj-