combined with bilirubin in preeclampsia (Master''s thesis) . Zhengzhou University, Zhengzhou, China: (2021). p. 1–33. [ Google Scholar ] 23. Yang SY, Fan L, Yin YP. Analysis of high-risk factors and prognostic influences for pregnant women with gestational diabetes mellitus complicated by preeclampsia. Mater Child Health Care China. (2021) 36(3):638–40. 10.19829/j.zgfybj.issn.1001-4411.2021.03.049 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Cai XH, Zhao LX, Li QH. Analysis on the occurrence and influencing factors of preeclampsia in patients with gestational diabetes mellitus. Clin Med Eng. (2021) 28(9):1291–2. 10.3969/j.issn.1674-4659.2021.09.1291 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Kim MJ, Kim HM, Cha HH, Seong WJ. Correlation between maternal weight gain in each trimester and fetal growth according to pre-pregnancy maternal body mass index in twin pregnancies. Medicina (Kaunas, Lithuania). (2022) 58(9):1209. 10.3390/medicina58091209 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Chuang YC, Huang L, Lee WY, Shaw SW, Chu FL, Hung TH. The association between weight gain at different stages of pregnancy and risk of gestational diabetes mellitus. J Diabetes Investig. (2022) 13(2):359–66. 10.1111/jdi.13648 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Peiqi CH, Zonglu YA, Ling ZH, Shigang DU, Lu YA, Shiyu LI, et al. Application of different assessment methods in cardiovascular disease risk assessment of T2DM. J Kunming Med Univ. (2022) 43(4):62–9. 10.12259/j.issn.2095-610X.S20220406 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Yu L, Xu XY. Construction and validation of a nomogram model for predicting adverse outcomes in early-onset severe preeclampsia among advanced-age pregnant women. J Clin Med Pract. (2023) 27(11):43–8, 79. 10.7619/jcmp.20223517 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Yue CY, Gao JP, Zhang CY, Ni YH, Ying CM. Development and validation of a nomogram for the early prediction of preeclampsia in pregnant Chinese women. Hypertens Res. (2021) 44(4):417–25. 10.1